    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town organized in 1854, and a post office opened in 1856 with John Clance as its first postmaster, linking settlers to distant offices.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pine_island_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1911 local dairies produced a world‑record 6,000‑pound cheese that rode a railroad flatcar, winning prizes and showcasing the town’s dairy pride.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
